{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they said, etc., lest He encounter us.</b> These words are Israel's. And although they said of blessed memory (Shemot Rabbah 5:14) that the elders slipped away one by one, nevertheless afterward they spoke these words. And because they did not come together with Moses and Aaron, they were punished. Or perhaps all the people entered together to Pharaoh and said to him words of reason, that it is better for him to let them go, for there is hope that afterward they will return from being there and be consumed by pestilence, etc.; moreover, this matter would cause Pharaoh to fear, for pestilence and sword reaching as far as his own dwelling would touch his heart. Or perhaps they contrived to frighten him lest He encounter Pharaoh, etc., and they clothed the curse within themselves for the sake of the king's honor."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:41.871561927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}